🔢 Day 32: Factorial Calculator — Loop + Recursive Versions

📌 Project Overview

Day 32 is part of Phase 3: Functions, File Handling, and Exceptions in my Python learning journey.

In this project, I built a factorial calculator using two different approaches:

Loop version: Uses a for loop to calculate the factorial.
Recursive version: Uses a function that calls itself to calculate the factorial.

Both functions calculate the factorial of the same number, allowing me to compare their results and understand the difference between loops and recursion.

The program also handles negative numbers and allows the user to calculate factorials repeatedly until they enter q to quit.

